I need to carefully design and write the builder and three levels. Let me write it.

Builder class:

```js
export const TILE = 48;
export const ROWS = 15;
export const WORLD_H = ROWS * TILE;

class LevelBuilder {
  constructor(cfg) {
    this.id=cfg.id; this.name=cfg.name; this.theme=cfg.theme; this.width=cfg.width;
    this.groundSegs=[]; this.platforms=[]; this.blocks=[]; this.pipes=[]; this.coins=[]; this.enemies=[]; this.movers=[]; this.springs=[]; this.decor=[];
    this.checkpointX=null; this.goalX=null; this.spawn={x:2.5,y:12};
  }
  ground(x0,x1,top=12){ this.groundSegs.push({x0,x1,top}); return this; }
  platform(x,y,w,h,type='stone'){ this.platforms.push({x,y,w,h,type}); return this; }
  block(x,y,type='?'){ this.blocks.push({x,y,type,used:false,bump:0}); return this; }
  pipe(x,top,h=2){ this.pipes.push({x,top,h,type:'pipe'}); return this; }
  coin(cx,cy){ this.coins.push({x:cx*TILE,y:cy*TILE,phase: ...}); } // centers in tiles
```
Hmm I planned coin(x,y) as cell index with center +0.5. Let me settle: coin(cx,cy) center in tile units. So to place above a block at cell x, y row 10, center y=10.5. I'll author with decimals like coin(cx, 10.5). That's more verbose but precise.

Helpers:
```js
coinRow(x, y, n, step=1, jitter=0) { for i: coin(x+0.5+i*step, y+0.5) } // x,y = cell indices
coinArc(x0, x1, yBase, yPeak, n) {
  for i 0..n-1: t=i/(n-1); cx = x0 + (x1-x0)*t; cy = yBase + (yPeak-yBase)*Math.sin(Math.PI*t)? 
}
```
Let me define `coinRow(x, y, n, step=1)` uses cell indices, center +0.5. `coinArc(x0,x1,yBase,yPeak,n)` uses cell indices, x from x0+0.25 to x1-0.25, y = yBase - (yBase-yPeak)*sin(pi*t) + 0.5. Good.

Enemy:
```js
enemy(x, surfaceRow, type='goomba', opts={}) {
  const w = type==='spiky'?36:38, h = type==='flyer'?30:32;
  this.enemies.push({cx:(x+0.5)*TILE, surfaceY:surfaceRow*TILE, type, ...opts});
}
```
For flyer, surfaceRow is center row: y=(surfaceRow+0.5)*TILE. I'll handle finalize.

Mover(x,y,w,h,axis,range,speed,phase=0): x,y,w,h cells; store.

spring(x,surfaceRow=12): x center px, y=surfaceRow*TILE.

checkpoint(x,surfaceRow): this.checkpointX = (x+0.5)*TILE; this.checkpointY = surfaceRow*TILE.

goal(x,surfaceRow): goalX=(x+0.5)*TILE; goalY=surfaceRow*TILE.

stairs(x, baseTop, steps, type='stone'): for i... platform(x+i, baseTop-i, 1, i+1, type). Note this creates overlapping solids? Adjacent columns don't overlap horizontally. Each column height grows; good.

Building solids:
```js
build(){
  const solids=[];
  for seg: push {x:seg.x0*TILE,y:seg.top*TILE,w:(seg.x1-seg.x0)*TILE,h:WORLD_H-seg.top*TILE,kind:'ground'}
  for p: {x:p.x*TILE,y:p.y*TILE,w:p.w*TILE,h:p.h*TILE,kind:'platform',type:p.type}
  for b: {x:b.x*TILE,y:b.y*TILE,w:TILE,h:TILE,kind:'block',block:b}
  for pipe: {x:pipe.x*TILE,y:pipe.top*TILE,w:2*TILE,h:pipe.h*TILE,kind:'pipe'}
  ...
}
```
Pipes h: height in tiles from top downwards. If top=10,h=2 → bottom at row12 = ground. Good. For pipes on other surfaces same.

Clock: coin phases deterministic.
Total coins = coins.length + blocks.filter(b=>b.type==='?').length.

Checkpoint spawn: if checkpoint then respawnX = checkpointX - 20, respawnY = checkpointY - PLAYER_H - 2, else spawn from this.spawn tile.

Level object includes `spawnX`, `spawnY`.

Ground gaps for rendering: compute from sorted ground segments:
```js
gaps=[]; sorted; for i< len-1: if next.x0 > seg.x1: gaps.push({x0:seg.x1, x1:next.x0});
```
Also maybe gap before first/after last none.

Total coin count ~? I'll count via node later.

Decor: builder add? Renderer generates deterministic bushes based on segments; no need.

