Now part 3: physics methods inserted before render or after syncHUD. Anchor `  render() {`. Add methods before render.

Methods:
- jumpSpeed, jumpMult
- updateMovers
- updatePlayer
- collideX, collideY
- doJump
- updateBlocks
- updateEnemies
- updateParticles, updateTexts
- spawn helpers: spawnDust, spawnBurst, spawnRing, spawnConfetti, addText
- collectCoin, gainCoin
- damage, pitFall, respawn
- beginClear, finishClear, beginGameOver
- overlap helpers, solidAt.

Need to write carefully.

`updateMovers`:
```js
updateMovers(dt){
 for(const m of this.level.movers){
  m.prevX=m.x; m.prevY=m.y;
  const off=Math.sin(this.levelTime*m.speed + m.phase)*m.range;
  if(m.axis==='x'){m.x=m.ox+off; m.y=m.oy;} else {m.x=m.ox; m.y=m.oy+off;}
  if(this.player && this.player.carrier===m){
   this.player.x += m.x-m.prevX;
   this.player.y += m.y-m.prevY;
  }
 }
 this.player.carrier=null;
}
```
Wait using this.levelTime before updatePlayer; levelTime incremented at update start. fine.

`updatePlayer(dt)`:
```js
const p=this.player, l=this.level;
p.prevY=p.y;
const dir=(this.input.right?1:0)-(this.input.left?1:0);
if(dir) p.facing=dir;
const accel = p.onGround?ACCEL:AIR_ACCEL;
if(dir!==0){
 const turnBonus = Math.sign(dir)!==Math.sign(p.vx)&&p.vx!==0 ? 1.6:1;
 p.vx += dir*accel*turnBonus*dt;
 p.vx = clamp(p.vx,-RUN_MAX*1.06,RUN_MAX*1.06);
}else{
 const fr=(p.onGround?FRICTION:FRICTION*0.32)*dt;
 p.vx=approach(p.vx,0,fr);
}
if(Math.abs(p.vx)>RUN_MAX) p.vx=approach(p.vx,Math.sign(p.vx)*RUN_MAX,1800*dt);

// jump buffer/coyote using previous ground
p.jumpBuffer=Math.max(0,p.jumpBuffer-dt);
const canJump = p.onGround || p.coyote>0;
if(p.jumpBuffer>0 && canJump) this.doJump();
p.coyote = p.onGround?COYOTE:Math.max(0,p.coyote-dt);

if(!p.onGround) p.vy += GRAVITY*dt; else p.vy += GRAVITY*dt; // always
p.vy=Math.min(p.vy,MAX_FALL);

const wasGrounded=p.onGround;
p.onGround=false;

// X
p.x += p.vx*dt;
this.collideX(p);
// Y
const fallSpeed=p.vy;
p.y += p.vy*dt;
this.collideY(p,fallSpeed);
// bounds
...
// landing squash if not wasGrounded and now onGround and fallSpeed>500
if(!wasGrounded && p.onGround && fallSpeed>420){ p.squash=Math.min(1,fallSpeed/1200); this.spawnDust(...); if(fallSpeed>900) this.shake=Math.max(this.shake,3); }
// coyote after
if(p.onGround) p.coyote=COYOTE;
// anim
p.anim += dt*(p.onGround? clamp(0.4+Math.abs(p.vx)/240,0.4,1.7):0.7);
p.squash=Math.max(0,p.squash-dt*4.2);
p.invuln=Math.max(0,p.invuln-dt);
p.springT=Math.max(0,p.springT-dt*3);
// dust
if(p.onGround && Math.abs(p.vx)>170){ p.dustT-=dt; if(p.dustT<=0){p.dustT=0.15; this.spawnDust(p.x+p.w/2 - Math.sign(p.vx)*8,p.y+p.h,2);} }
// collect coins
...
// checkpoints
...
// goal
if(this.level.goal && p.x+p.w>this.level.goal.x-16){ this.beginClear(); return; }
// fall
if(p.y>l.worldH+150){ this.pitFall(); return; }
```
Wait order of gravity: if onGround and standing, gravity adds vy then collideY resolves to 0 each frame. Fine. But jump check happens before gravity; doJump sets vy. Then gravity added same frame reduces jump slightly; standard. But I call doJump before adding gravity — jump velocity then gravity; fine.

However canJump uses p.onGround from previous frame. After doJump, p.onGround=false, p.jumpBuffer=0. Then later `p.onGround=false` again. Fine.

`collideY` requires p.vy sign: after gravity, vy positive when standing even though onGround; resolves; sets onGround true.

Collision X before Y; good.

Clamp x:
```js
if(p.x<0){p.x=0;p.vx=Math.max(0,p.vx);}
if(p.x+p.w>l.worldW){p.x=l.worldW-p.w;p.vx=Math.min(0,p.vx);}
if(p.y<0){p.y=0; if(p.vy<0)p.vy=0;}
```
If player falls, no upper clamp issue.

